+# Native DSETUP loading and truthful version metadata source repair
+
+Implemented against canonical remote main `89f1e9d2c67aa94d56d2319115589d07204d42e0`, verified with actual canonical HTTPS `ls-remote` before checkout and before publication. Branch: `task/shadow-man-dsetup-native-version-repair-oct22`. Final commit/actual remote verification are recorded in `publication.json` and the append-only root messageboard. No main merge.
+
+## Implementation
+
+`lib/dll-registry.js` now allows **installed app-local DSETUP.DLL** through the shared native dependency graph. There is no bundled download path, ordinal alias, replacement handler or executable patch. DSETUP32/16 are not newly allowlisted: they are not static dependencies of this version-reader call. Existing DSETUP static imports and all other real-PE and child lookup paths remain unchanged.
+
+`GetFileVersionInfoSizeA` and `GetFileVersionInfoA` now always use the existing named-file resource reader, as their W counterparts already did. A static DirectX basename no longer overrides a real file or returns canned metadata when no resource exists. The fabricated `$DX_VERSION_INFO` initializer was removed; its region and globals remain reserved, avoiding unrelated region moves and generated-map changes. Return values, DWORD handle writes, length-bounded copies and stdcall cleanup continue through the existing helpers/epilogues. No new last-error contract is invented: the unchanged named-file reader/host filesystem determines existing failure/error behavior.
+
+The shared boot helper retains DirectX file-presence placeholders and `staticModule` loader exclusion, but gives them **no RT_VERSION**. This covers DDRAW, DSOUND, DPLAYX, D3DRM and D3D8 rather than leaving another invented DirectX fallback. Real installed entries are preserved. Previously retained placeholders explicitly marked `staticModule` are refreshed idempotently, so their old version resources cannot survive a normal mount. Unrelated OpenGL placeholder/version behavior is preserved, not qualified by this task.
+
+`lib/storage.js` no longer seeds a fabricated DirectX `Version`/`InstalledVersion` registry key. Ordinary missing-key/value behavior therefore survives in fresh/reset state. Installer-supplied and imported registry values remain normal metadata, read verbatim with existing A/W encoding and buffer/error semantics. No runtime-support policy or minimum-version assertion was added.
+
+**Persisted-state limit:** old registry snapshots have no provenance marker distinguishing a previous synthetic default from an installer writing the same string. This change does not delete existing values by guessing from their numeric content, or claim those values prove an installed/capable runtime. Likewise an imported file without the synthetic marker is treated as a supplied file, not classified by version number. The actual stopped installation's registry is unavailable here: its current branch, value and eventual native detector output remain unknown. Inspection of that exact preserved state belongs to coordinator qualification; no snapshot was queried or modified.
+
+## Acceptance evidence
+
+Run from this checkout:
+
+```sh
+GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1 python3 scratch/runs/20261022-shadow-man-dsetup-native-version-repair/verify.py
+```
+
+`checks.json` records exact commands, exit statuses, output and elapsed times. All **23 commands pass**, including:
+
+- Existing storage/registry suite, plus new DirectX registry absence/supplied-value tests: case-insensitive lookup, REG_SZ A/W byte counts and terminators, undersized-buffer `ERROR_MORE_DATA` with unchanged canaries, missing InstalledVersion `ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND`, snapshot restore, and reset without reseeding.
+- Existing `test-file-version-info.js` in explicit `--source-fixture` mode: named-file PE resource parsing, absent/malformed resource handling, bounded short copies, hierarchy/languages/translation, string lifetime, ANSI and Unicode queries and malformed-child rejection. Optional sealed native inputs additionally compare actual DSETUP and DSETUP32 RT_VERSION bytes verbatim through the DDRAW filename, both A/W, with four-byte output canaries and root fixed-info size 52. Authentic config has no resource and correctly fails without writing output. Aliasing these setup/config bytes to DDRAW is solely a **test fixture**, not installing them as runtime files or asserting their versions describe DirectX capabilities.
+- Existing DirectX system-file test in explicit source-fixture mode: file attributes/presence, preserved supplied file, refreshed known synthetic snapshot, idempotence, CLI static-module byte-lookup exclusion, no invented A/W DirectX version, zero DWORD handle, unchanged failed-output buffers and ret+args increments 12/20. The full-host `has_dll_file` assertion remains in default mode but is explicitly omitted in this small fixture; no browser qualification is claimed.
+- New loader regression with tiny source images and separately the **sealed original D3DConfigUtility.exe and DSETUP.DLL**. The real JS graph selects authentic bytes; missing-file and wrong-name controls fail selection. Verbatim production WAT `parse_exports`, `patch_caller_iat`, `resolve_ordinal`/locked reader and name matching are compiled into a small standalone fixture. The actual production JS `patchExeImports` then reaches those WAT functions and binds original IAT **0x409024 to 0x100018b0**. Missing EAT slot and out-of-range ordinal controls return no binding. Named/CRT/thunk detours deliberately trap in this ordinal-only fixture. Mapping is a source fixture's section copy; allocator/lifecycle/lock boundaries are substitutes. This does **not** qualify full `load_dll`, DllMain, concurrency, PE relocation or native x86 execution.
+- Four semantic rejecting controls: restore exact baseline DLL registry (skipped load); exact baseline process-boot helper (synthetic file versions); exact baseline storage module (synthetic registry); exact baseline ANSI handlers and DX block in the focused VERSION fixture (by-name fabrication). Each reaches an AssertionError, not a compiler/setup failure. `mutation-results.json` retains diagnostics. The old ANSI classifier boundary is fixed to this test's known DirectX path; handlers and data are the exact old source.
+- Changed JS syntax; both changed WAT fragments' parentheses/labels; logical-AND check on the materialized relevant source subset; explicit-path Git whitespace check; evidence containment checker (no invalid or missing artifacts). ShadowMan remains intentionally unregistered; no misleading dashboard `result.json` is attached to another candidate.
+
+The accepted donor `504f904510ffeedea6c9824c992788db30ea76d1` already establishes the native optional DWORD-output wrapper, BOOL=1 even with zero detection and `ret 8`; its evidence was reused, not re-analyzed. All four original seals are checked before the native graph probe. No API table or native wrapper changed. Neither these fixtures nor this report claim that wrapper executed. No guest, fullmodule or historical f644bbb2 Wasm was used.
+
+## Compatibility and remaining qualification
+
+Software that previously passed prerequisites solely on synthesized DX6.1a/DX7/DX8.1 metadata can now warn or fail. That is intentional: the prerequisite may remain failing when no actual metadata exists. Authentic existing resources are still readable regardless of whether their capabilities are implemented. Numeric metadata is not capability qualification. File presence and static dispatch remain available, and unrelated DLL policy/child execution paths were not refactored.
+
+Default full-emulator versions of `test-static-dx-version.js` (updated to expect named-file behavior), DirectX setup/ordinal tests, NE version tests and full PE lifecycle/import tests were **not run** because this task prohibits a full build/runtime. Cheap source checks and focused fixtures do not replace them. Coordinator owns independent review, exact canonical build and runtime qualification, including native initialization and actual registry/OS/fallback selection. There is no gameplay, successful prerequisite, supported DirectX version, installation or user-interface claim.
+
+## Recovery, resources and operational limits
+
+`source-pins.json` records exact base blob/SHA/size/source for the focused verified files. Historical root files were accepted only when byte-identical to those pins; no fetch/lazy-fetch, broad checkout or source-version substitution occurred. Own `.git` was copied into an isolated thin checkout and its index reset to the complete base tree; only named files are staged, never sparse absences. Baseline blobs needed for scoped diff were written only to own object database. An initial unscoped Git diff failed on the intentionally incomplete object store (no retained core); subsequent review uses explicit paths and stored pinned blobs. The normal commit command also required an unrelated missing base blob (lib/agent-connect-ui.js), so publication uses `git write-tree --missing-ok` and `git commit-tree` from the reviewed explicit index, preserving the complete base tree. The initial push after that failed commit created only the unchanged-base task ref; the implementation updates it by ordinary fast-forward, never force. Root/donor HEAD/index/config/alternates remain sealed against the accepted donor's earlier metadata receipt.
+
+`resources.json` counts own Git/source/artifacts, shared read-only native inputs, launcher directory/task prompt, **8 MiB reserve inside 64 MiB**, and a further 4 MiB publication allowance. It enforces host free floor 2982150144 bytes. This task used no obsolete 16 MiB subcap. Final publication remeasures allocation and records actual remote refs.
+
+No native binary is committed or duplicated. See RECOVERY.md for original paths and commands. No runtime, new compute, rebuild, reinstall, extraction, download, public deployment, laptop, other game, approval or other worker actions occurred. **All boxes remain stopped**: coordinator evidence says bx_m4xrrj5a snapshot-stop completed 2026-10-22T20:31:48.291Z (previous expiry 21:52:45.530Z). No lifecycle query/action occurred here; coordinator retains ownership. One bounded task ends at publication.
